SYNC(2)                        P32W Unix                         SYNC(2)

NAME
       sync - write out the buffer cache

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       void sync(void);

DESCRIPTION
       sync writes every modified block in the buffer cache to its
       disk, and the superblock of every mounted filesystem. It
       returns when the writes are done. The kernel does the same
       by itself every 30 seconds. Call it (or sync(1)) before
       turning the machine off; reboot(2) does it too, and also
       marks the filesystems clean.

       sync leaves the filesystems marked as in use, so that
       fsck(8) checks them after a crash.

SEE ALSO
       sync(1), reboot(2), mount(2), fsck(8)

BUGS
       None known; unlike V7's, P32W's sync waits for the writes to
       finish.
